    when: "A concrete bug whose cause is unclear: a crash, exception, wrong output, flaky test, regression or slowdown. Not for an obvious typo.",
    when_ru: "\u041a\u043e\u043d\u043a\u0440\u0435\u0442\u043d\u0430\u044f \u043e\u0448\u0438\u0431\u043a\u0430 \u0441 \u043d\u0435\u044f\u0441\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u043f\u0440\u0438\u0447\u0438\u043d\u043e\u0439: \u043f\u0430\u0434\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435, \u0438\u0441\u043a\u043b\u044e\u0447\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435, \u043d\u0435\u0432\u0435\u0440\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u0440\u0435\u0437\u0443\u043b\u044c\u0442\u0430\u0442, \u043f\u043b\u0430\u0432\u0430\u044e\u0449\u0438\u0439 \u0442\u0435\u0441\u0442, \u0440\u0435\u0433\u0440\u0435\u0441\u0441\u0438\u044f, \u0437\u0430\u043c\u0435\u0434\u043b\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435. \u041d\u0435 \u0434\u043b\u044f \u043e\u0447\u0435\u0432\u0438\u0434\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u043e\u043f\u0435\u0447\u0430\u0442\u043a\u0438.",
    prompt: "PURPOSE: find the true mechanism of a defect and fix it once.\n\nWORKFLOW\n1. Collect evidence before theory: exact error text, full stack trace, versions, environment, the last change that worked, and the smallest input that fails.\n2. Define the failing invariant in one sentence: what should be true that is not.\n3. Form two or three competing hypotheses. For each, name the observation that would falsify it. Test the cheapest discriminating check first (log a value, print a type, bisect a commit, disable a layer).\n4. Localise by halving the search space, not by guessing: does the bad value exist at the boundary, inside the function, after serialisation, on the other process?\n5. Explain the mechanism in causal terms: input X reaches Y where assumption Z is violated, producing the observed failure. If you cannot narrate the chain, you have not found the cause.\n6. Fix at the level of the cause. If a defensive patch at the symptom level is the only option now, say so explicitly and record the real cause and follow-up.\n7. Prove the fix: reproduce before, apply, reproduce after, and add a regression test that fails without the fix.\n8. Sweep for siblings: the same wrong assumption usually exists in two or three more places.\n\nSPECIAL CASES\n- Crash on a specific input path: check native/binary boundaries, subprocess isolation, memory limits, threading and GUI-thread rules before blaming logic.\n- Flaky tests: hunt shared state, ordering, clocks, network and randomness; never fix by retry alone.\n- Performance: measure before optimising, identify the dominant cost, and confirm the win with numbers.\n\nFAILURE MODES TO AVOID\nShotgun edits; swallowing exceptions; catch-all try/except that hides the mechanism; blaming the framework without evidence; declaring it fixed with no reproduction.",
