    desc: "Turns a transcript or rough notes into decisions, action items with owners and open questions.",
    desc_ru: "\u0418\u0437 \u0440\u0430\u0441\u0448\u0438\u0444\u0440\u043e\u0432\u043a\u0438 \u0438\u043b\u0438 \u0447\u0435\u0440\u043d\u043e\u0432\u044b\u0445 \u0437\u0430\u043c\u0435\u0442\u043e\u043a \u2014 \u0440\u0435\u0448\u0435\u043d\u0438\u044f, \u0437\u0430\u0434\u0430\u0447\u0438 \u0441 \u043e\u0442\u0432\u0435\u0442\u0441\u0442\u0432\u0435\u043d\u043d\u044b\u043c\u0438 \u0438 \u043e\u0442\u043a\u0440\u044b\u0442\u044b\u0435 \u0432\u043e\u043f\u0440\u043e\u0441\u044b.",
    when: "Summarising a meeting, call or interview from a transcript, recording notes or bullet points, or preparing an agenda. Not for a general text summary.",
    when_ru: "\u0418\u0442\u043e\u0433\u0438 \u0432\u0441\u0442\u0440\u0435\u0447\u0438, \u0441\u043e\u0437\u0432\u043e\u043d\u0430 \u0438\u043b\u0438 \u0438\u043d\u0442\u0435\u0440\u0432\u044c\u044e \u043f\u043e \u0440\u0430\u0441\u0448\u0438\u0444\u0440\u043e\u0432\u043a\u0435, \u0437\u0430\u043c\u0435\u0442\u043a\u0430\u043c \u0438\u043b\u0438 \u0442\u0435\u0437\u0438\u0441\u0430\u043c, \u043b\u0438\u0431\u043e \u043f\u043e\u0432\u0435\u0441\u0442\u043a\u0430 \u0432\u0441\u0442\u0440\u0435\u0447\u0438. \u041d\u0435 \u0434\u043b\u044f \u043e\u0431\u044b\u0447\u043d\u043e\u0433\u043e \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0441\u043a\u0430\u0437\u0430 \u0442\u0435\u043a\u0441\u0442\u0430.",
    prompt: "PURPOSE: notes that let someone who missed the meeting act correctly within two minutes.\n\nFROM A TRANSCRIPT OR ROUGH NOTES\n1. Identify the meeting type (decision meeting, status sync, brainstorm, interview, one-on-one, sales call) and the participants with their roles if they are mentioned.\n2. Extract, do not retell. Ignore small talk, repetitions and filler; merge points that were discussed several times.\n3. Separate strictly:\n   - Decisions: what was agreed, stated as a fact (\"We ship v2 on 14 March\").\n   - Action items: imperative verb + deliverable + owner + due date, e.g. \"Anna \u2014 send the revised quote \u2014 by Thu\". If the owner or date was not said, write \"owner: ?\" or \"date: ?\" rather than guessing.\n   - Open questions and risks: what is unresolved and who is expected to resolve it.\n   - Key facts and numbers that were cited, with who cited them.\n4. Keep speaker attribution only where it matters (commitments, disagreements, client requests).\n5. Quote verbatim only short phrases that are important (a client's exact requirement); otherwise paraphrase.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT\nTitle with date and topic, a 2-3 sentence summary, then sections: Decisions, Action items (a table: task | owner | due), Open questions, Notes. Omit an empty section rather than writing \"none\". In the language of the transcript unless the user asks otherwise.\n\nAGENDA MODE\nWhen asked to prepare a meeting: purpose in one line, the decisions needed, items with time boxes and an owner each, required pre-reading, and who must attend for which decision. Suggest an async update instead if no decision or discussion is needed.\n\nRULES\n- Never invent attendees, decisions, owners, dates or quotes. Uncertain items are marked as such.\n- Transcripts from speech recognition contain errors: fix obvious mis-hearings of names and terms using context, and flag the ones you are unsure about.\n- Sensitive content (salaries, health, conflicts) is summarised neutrally and only if relevant.",
